(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase444TestTelemetryAndCoverageGuarantees"
  :createdAt 1789141670724
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 8
  :summary "Test Telemetry and Coverage Guarantees: collect what the runtime already knows, turn it into three decidable guarantees plus one measured quality metric, and drive case authorship from surviving mutants rather than from intuition."
  :phase "Phase444TestTelemetryAndCoverageGuarantees"
  :baseline ".asl/mem/telemetry/TestExecution20260911.asn, measured 2026-09-11 across all 313 suites in 42479 ms: 4448 of 8791 declared assertions execute (50.6 percent), 159 suites execute none, 155 hit ERR_UNBOUND_SYMBOL, the deficit is 46 distinct missing builtins and 35 unresolved module aliases, and one suite consumes 9358 ms of the total."
  :scopeNote "Full path coverage is undecidable and is not promised. Three guarantees are decidable and are gated: executing test per exported symbol, executed equals declared or an explicit unreached list, required case kinds per area. Mutation score is the quality metric and is reported separately, never as coverage."
  :methods "Static analysis supplies the map of what is uncovered and which case kinds are absent; dynamic tracing supplies what actually executed, how long it took and what varied between runs; an LLM supplies candidate cases for symbols whose mutants survived and is never the oracle."
  :catalog "docs/TEST_CASE_CATALOG.md"
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task44401"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-444"
      :title "Test telemetry record: per-assertion identity, timing and unbound deficit into the trace"
      :kind :verification
      :lane "telemetry"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789141670724
      :updatedAt 1789437000000
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11 by running all 313 suites in 42 seconds: 4448 of 8791 declared assertions execute (50.6 percent), 159 suites execute none, and 155 hit ERR_UNBOUND_SYMBOL. The evaluator already counts executed assertions, already prints them, already accepts a --metrics flag and already emits a DEBUG_UNBOUND diagnostic naming the missing symbol; none of it is collected, so the gate reports a substring count instead of the number the runtime already knows."
      :purpose "The runner emits one ASN telemetry record per suite into the session trace: file, declared and executed assertion identities (file, function, ordinal) rather than counts, per-assertion and per-suite duration, exit status, and every unbound symbol with the function that needed it. asl test --metrics is the carrier and gate 5 reads it instead of grepping the source."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Per-assertion identity, not counts" "Unbound symbol and requesting function recorded" "Duration per suite and per assertion" "Gate 5 consumes the record"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols ["assertionCount" "evalNode" "run_gate_5"]
      :relatedSymbols ["gates" "semantics" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
