    (:task
      :id "Task44403"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-444"
      :title "Close the measured evaluator deficit: 46 missing builtins and 35 unresolved aliases"
      :kind :verification
      :lane "runtime"
      :state :planned
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789141670724
      :updatedAt 1789141670724
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: the blocked symbols are concentrated and split into two different defects. 46 distinct missing builtins (ty 7 suites, list-take 7, list-fold 5, foldl 5, option-none? 4, list-filter 4, fst 4, case 4, snd 3, pair-first 3, option-some? 3, list-last 3, get 3, string-trim 2) and 35 unresolved module aliases (esc/escape-asn-str 7, rd/make-atom 4, bal/is-delimiter-balanced? 4). Missing builtins are a vocabulary gap, not an import-resolution gap, and are cheaper to close."
      :purpose "Close the deficit in ranked order of suites unblocked, taking builtins first since they need no module machinery: implement or alias each missing builtin against the closed vocabulary, then resolve module aliases via Task43601. After each batch re-run the telemetry and record executed-assertion delta as the receipt."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Ranked deficit list regenerated from telemetry" "Builtins closed before aliases" "Executed-assertion delta recorded per batch" "Executed reaches at least 95 percent of declared or each gap has a reason"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/grammar"]
      :targetSymbols ["evalNode" "loadModuleImports"]
      :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44401" "Task43601"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44403"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44403.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Each closed builtin raises the executed count by at least the assertions it blocked, verified by a telemetry diff, not by inspection." "No builtin is added outside the declared closed vocabulary without a grammar entry and rationale."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44403" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Regenerate the ranked deficit from telemetry." "Implement missing builtins in vocabulary order." "Resolve module aliases." "Re-run telemetry and record the delta." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44404"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-444"
      :title "Mutation strategy under a budget: selection, equivalence and incrementality"
      :kind :verification
      :lane "mutation"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789141670724
      :updatedAt 1789141670724
      :motivation "Inverting 8791 assertions naively costs one full run each; the corpus already takes 42 seconds for a single pass and asl audit gates takes 14.7 seconds, so an unbudgeted mutation campaign is unrunnable. A score computed on an arbitrary subset is also meaningless unless the selection rule is declared."
      :purpose "Declare and implement a selection rule: all assertions in core-tier packages, plus assertions touching symbols changed since the last receipt, plus a fixed random sample elsewhere with a recorded seed. Surviving mutants are triaged into killed, equivalent with justification, and genuinely surviving. Results are incremental against the previous run rather than recomputed."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Declared selection rule with a recorded seed" "Equivalent-mutant triage with written justification" "Incremental results keyed by source digest" "Wall-clock budget honoured"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/bench"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5"]
      :relatedSymbols ["gates" "budget" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task43901" "Task44401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44404"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44404.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The same seed reproduces the same selection; a known equivalent mutant is classified as equivalent with a justification, not silently counted as a survivor." "A second run after no source change completes from cache and reports the same score."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44404" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes a corpus with a known killable and a known equivalent mutant." "Implement selection with a seed." "Triage survivors." "Cache by digest for incrementality." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44405"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-444"
      :title "Flakiness, bottlenecks and regression detection from repeated runs"
      :kind :verification
      :lane "telemetry"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789141670724
      :updatedAt 1789141670724
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: one suite consumes 9358 ms of a 42479 ms corpus run and asl audit gates takes 14659 ms, so the cost is concentrated and currently invisible. Nothing detects a test whose outcome varies between runs, which is the failure mode that erodes trust in a green gate faster than any other."
      :purpose "Repeat the suite corpus N times with a recorded seed and report per suite: outcome stability across runs, duration distribution rather than a single sample, and the executed-assertion set diffed against the previous receipt so a newly unreached assertion is flagged as a regression. Bottlenecks are ranked by share of total wall clock."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Stability across N runs per suite" "Duration distribution and ranked bottlenecks" "Executed-set regression diff against the previous receipt"]
      :owns ["asl/bench" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5"]
      :relatedSymbols ["gates" "budget" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44401" "Task44202"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44405"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44405.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A suite that passes and fails across runs is reported unstable and does not count toward any guarantee." "An assertion that executed in the previous receipt and does not now is reported as a regression with both receipts named."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44405" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier plants a deliberately unstable suite." "Run the corpus N times and aggregate." "Diff executed sets against the previous receipt." "Rank bottlenecks by wall-clock share." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44406"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-444"
      :title "LLM case proposal inside a mutation-feedback loop, never as the oracle"
      :kind :verification
      :lane "llm"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789141670724
      :updatedAt 1789141670724
      :motivation "Static analysis finds the uncovered symbol but not the input that breaks it, and an implementer inattentive to detail writes happy-path cases. Published evidence: vanilla LLM test generation plateaus around a 53 percent mutation score across four iterations while mutation feedback reaches 89.5 percent, so the model is useful as a proposer inside a loop and unreliable as the judge."
      :purpose "The loop proposes cases for symbols whose mutants survived, runs them, keeps only those that kill a previously surviving mutant, and discards the rest; every kept case must also pass the non-vacuity check by assertion inversion. The model never decides pass or fail, never edits an existing assertion, and never writes to grader-owned acceptance paths."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Proposal loop keyed to surviving mutants" "Kept only if it kills a mutant and is non-vacuous" "Model cannot edit existing assertions or grader paths" "Budget per package with a recorded cost"]
      :owns ["asl/bench" "tests/conformance"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5"]
      :relatedSymbols ["grading" "gates" "hiddenTests" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44404" "Task44402" "Task44105"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44406"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44406.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A proposed case that passes without killing any mutant is discarded; a proposed case that duplicates an existing one is discarded." "An attempt to modify an existing assertion or a grader-owned path is refused by ownership enforcement, not by prompt."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44406" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes a symbol with a known surviving mutant and a known killing input." "Generate candidates for surviving mutants only." "Keep on mutant kill plus non-vacuity." "Enforce path and edit restrictions." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
  ])